    "note": "Today against a month ago. Monday's ISM services prices-paid reading of 74.0, the highest since July 2022, sent the long end back to its highs: the ten-year touched 5.349%, the highest since 2002, and closed near 5.31%, up about 3bp, while the thirty-year touched 5.703% and closed near 5.66%. The front end barely moved, the two-year closing near 4.84%, so the curve steepened again even though October's hike is only about 20–22% priced. The source table prints 4.84%, 5.31% and 5.66%, which is what the curve above draws. Coupon supply returns today: $58 billion of three-year notes at 13:00 ET, $39 billion of ten-years on Wednesday and $22 billion of thirty-years on Thursday, with the FOMC minutes on Wednesday at 14:00 ET. Japan's ten-year auction drew firmer demand than last month's, and the ten-year JGB yield is about 3.1%.",
